Thanks to all in thread!!!

I admit to not knowing about expand_dump.  I used it, it worked.

I also corrected my dbx syntax, and used the line TL gave.  Finding
pages on Google before gave the lines I quoted before, which proved
less than useful.

Again, thanks to all!!  And to recap, the crashes SEEM to be actually
from a network driver on the gigabit, not the SCSI talking to the RAID
array.  I was blaming a new RAID, when it seems I should blame Chinese
kids and bad tcp packets.  Okay, and my own stupidity.

This system has a public adapter.  No firewall in front (did I mention
my own stupidity?)  SSH and SSL only allowed inside, but that did not
seem to help, because either 1) massive SSH hits caused it to crash,
or 2) bad tcp packets cause it to crash.  Or both.  Using pf on the
interface and blocking all IPs seen in China, Korea and Taiwan has
rectified the issue (no crashes in 40+ days!!!).

A very good transparent firewall going in front of this system RSN.

Thanks again!

-- robert


